name 'designing-reliable-apps-postassessment-q14_2025'

question 'A developer builds a news app that fetches headlines from an external API. When the API fails, the app displays locally stored "popular stories from last week" with a note: "Live news unavailable — showing recent highlights." What pattern does this implement?'

right 'A hybrid architecture with a local fallback — using local data to maintain a useful experience when live data is unavailable'
wrong 'A try/catch fallback — using the catch block to retry the API request with different parameters'
wrong 'A loading state — temporarily showing local data while waiting for the API to respond'
wrong 'An empty state — displaying placeholder content while the app initializes'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 10
